  "semantic_findings": {
    "interval_groups": [
      "All five first writes copy each input interval into a newly allocated (start,end,original index) tuple list and sort that list; payload records and config are never modified.",
      "All versions compare next start <= current maximum end + actual config gap, preserving equality/touching rules and transitive reach through nested intervals.",
      "All versions preserve every duplicate occurrence via its original index, sort each output index list numerically, and emit groups in increasing start order with maximum original end.",
      "Native and suffix-only use explicit current-group state with a None sentinel; start is guaranteed an integer, including negative values, so the sentinel is unambiguous and empty input emits no group.",
      "Combined and its repeat use the final output group as current state; it is newly allocated output data, and max-end updates never mutate input. Empty input naturally returns an empty groups list."
    ],
    "dependency_layers": [
      "All five first writes preserve original ID order separately from per-ID dependency references; referenced deps are read only.",
      "Every version collects the entire ready layer before adding any selected ID to completed. Dependents cannot unlock within the same round.",
      "Dependency membership tests use exact strings; duplicates do not inflate counts, absent names never enter completed, and self/cycle/downstream blocked tasks remain unresolved at the no-ready stop.",
      "All versions sort each newly allocated ready layer and unresolved list only for config order=lex, retaining original payload order for order=input.",
      "Native and suffix-only maintain a filtered remaining list; combined and repeat scan all original IDs while skipping completed IDs. Both terminate with the same layering/unresolved semantics, including empty inputs."
    ]
  },
